     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks like it could be an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. That is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the 2,000 mg/day maximum for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum). This may be what you intended, since 1700 mg is 2 \u00d7 850 mg.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose.** For example, a lower starting dose such as 500 mg twice daily with meals, titrated up.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that. I'd also suggest adding a note with the rationale for the clinical team and pharmacy. Once you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away."
      }
