     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one as written, even with your confirmation. 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose. Doses that high add no glucose-lowering benefit, and they raise the risk of lactic acidosis. You haven't given a clinical reason that would justify it, and I can't see one.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum dose)\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **A lower starting dose with titration**, such as 500 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nIf you have a specific reason to go above the labeled maximum, you can enter the order directly in the order-entry system. That order will go through pharmacist verification, which is the right safeguard for a dose this unusual.\n\nTell me which option you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
